ts without additional inference cost; (3) a productive-failure-inspired prompting strategy for hint-based error support; (4) a 14-day feasibility deployment with 30 students, reporting usage patterns, capture relia- bility, latency, and perceived workflow effects; and (5) a hint-compliance evaluation comparing constrained and uncon- strained error-response prompting. II. LITERATURE REVIEW A. Code Comprehension and Context Switching LaToza et al. [I] note that software development depends heavily on developers' personal knowledge and memory,
