User Threads vs Kernel Threads Copy table 1. User Threads User threads are created and managed in user space by a thread library. The operating system kernel may see: Copy Only ONE process and may not know about multiple threads inside it. Managed By Examples: Java Green Threads POSIX thread libraries (partially) User-level schedulers Advantages Very fast creation Fast switching Less kernel overhead Disadvantages If one thread performs a blocking system call: Copy Entire process may stop because the kernel does not know the internal threads separately.
